## Coupled oscillator theory

### the Kuramoto model

<aside class="notes">
7:00-9:00 -- THE TURN. Name it: this is mathematics, a real active
research area. Check the metronomes here, live, in front of the room.
If they haven't locked in step yet: say so, let the tension sit
("they're not there yet -- watch"). If they HAVE synced already,
that's a genuine "it happened while we were talking" moment --
better than anything staged.
</aside>

---

<div class="r-fit-text">
Watch it happen.
</div>

<aside class="notes">
9:00-18:00 -- CENTREPIECE, longest section by design, don't rush once
running. Advance to the next slide -- the Sync Dial is built straight
into this deck now, so there's no switching to another window or
tab. Drag the coupling slider K from low to high, live, and let the
room watch the order parameter r climb from near 0 toward 1 as the
oscillators lock into phase. The "New starting phases" button gives
you a fresh, unsynchronised starting point if you want to run it a
second time. Come back to this deck for the next slide once the room
has seen it happen.
</aside>

