## Why this is a maths degree

<aside class="notes">
18:00-25:00 -- WIDEN THE LENS. Zoom out from the demo to why this is
a maths degree, not a party trick. Make each of the next four beats
personal and quick, not a module list.
</aside>

---

### Differential equations

The metronomes' motion is, quite literally, a system of them.

---

### Complex analysis

The order parameter *r* you just watched *is* a complex number --
its size is "how in sync," its angle is "the shared rhythm."

---

### Dynamical systems & bifurcation

Below a critical coupling strength, synchrony never happens.\
Above it, it suddenly does.\
That sudden flip has a name: a bifurcation.

---

### Network science

Real synchronising systems -- power grids, neurons, cardiac tissue,
the fireflies -- aren't tidy pairs. They're networks. Whether they
sync at all depends on the *shape* of the network.

---

